## Pipeline

[`{{ d }}sources.toml`]({{ d }}sources.toml) declares every input: its URL, its reuse
terms, and whether the pipeline reads it yet (`status`). `just fetch` downloads each
implemented source to `{{ d }}data/raw/` with a fetch record. `just build` writes
`{{ d }}data/processed/`. `just validate` checks the published output against the fetch
records. Neither directory goes into git. [ATTRIBUTION.md](ATTRIBUTION.md) lists what
this repository reuses, and on what terms.
{% endif %}{% if 'ts' in stacks and ts_kind == 'web-app' %}{% set d = '' if ts_dir == '.' else ts_dir ~ '/' %}
## Deploy

`pnpm{% if ts_dir != '.' %} -C {{ ts_dir }}{% endif %} dev` serves the app with live reload. Cloudflare Pages deploys it through its Git
integration: create a Pages project from this repository, with build command
`pnpm build`{% if ts_dir != '.' %}, root directory `{{ ts_dir }}`{% endif %} and output directory `dist`. Every push to `main` deploys, and
every pull request gets a preview URL. [`{{ d }}public/_headers`]({{ d }}public/_headers) sets the
response headers, including the Content-Security-Policy that the e2e tests run under.
{% endif %}
